1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,714
Coach: A reply can sound relevant because it mentions the same topic,

2
00:00:04,714 --> 00:00:07,715
Coach: yet miss the point someone has made.

3
00:00:07,715 --> 00:00:09,857
Coach: Before preparing your next sentence,

4
00:00:09,857 --> 00:00:12,429
Coach: notice what their contribution actually contains.

5
00:00:12,779 --> 00:00:17,922
Coach: Imagine a group planning a thirty-minute paper-folding workshop for beginners.

6
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:20,922
Coach: There is one facilitator and shared materials.

7
00:00:20,922 --> 00:00:26,493
Coach: The aim is to give participants an opportunity to try and ask questions.

8
00:00:26,493 --> 00:00:28,636
Coach: No workshop has taken place.

9
00:00:28,986 --> 00:00:34,129
Noah: I would keep the demonstration brief, so people have time to try.

10
00:00:34,129 --> 00:00:39,700
Noah: I am worried that someone who misses a step could get left behind.

11
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:44,764
Coach: Noah offers a proposal, explains its purpose, and raises a concern.

12
00:00:44,764 --> 00:00:47,336
Coach: These are useful things to notice,

13
00:00:47,336 --> 00:00:51,193
Coach: rather than three boxes that every speaker must fill.

14
00:00:51,543 --> 00:00:54,972
Coach: His proposal is to keep the demonstration brief.

15
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:57,543
Coach: That does not mean removing it.

16
00:00:57,543 --> 00:01:00,971
Coach: The word brief limits the time spent demonstrating;

17
00:01:00,971 --> 00:01:04,400
Coach: it does not tell us an exact duration.

18
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:09,036
Coach: His reason is to leave time for people to try.

19
00:01:09,036 --> 00:01:11,607
Coach: This connects to the workshop aim.

20
00:01:11,607 --> 00:01:17,607
Coach: He has explained why the proposal may matter, without showing that it will work.

21
00:01:17,957 --> 00:01:20,528
Coach: Look at those two parts separately.

22
00:01:20,528 --> 00:01:26,528
Coach: Which tells the group what Noah suggests, and which explains why he suggests it?

23
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:29,528
Coach: Think about the link before moving on.

24
00:01:37,878 --> 00:01:41,307
Coach: Keeping the demonstration brief is the proposed action.

25
00:01:41,307 --> 00:01:44,307
Coach: Leaving time to try is its reason.

26
00:01:44,307 --> 00:01:49,878
Coach: Hearing both helps you respond to the proposal in relation to the task.

27
00:01:50,228 --> 00:01:55,800
Coach: The concern is different: someone who misses a step could get left behind.

28
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,514
Coach: Noah names a possibility.

29
00:01:57,514 --> 00:02:03,514
Coach: He has not said that every beginner will struggle or that anyone already has.

30
00:02:03,864 --> 00:02:06,864
Coach: This concern does not cancel his proposal.

31
00:02:06,864 --> 00:02:12,436
Coach: It leaves a question about how to support someone who misses a step.

32
00:02:12,436 --> 00:02:17,150
Coach: For now, keep that question open instead of inventing his solution.

33
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,643
Coach: You also do not know how Noah feels about the whole plan.

34
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:24,786
Coach: His words identify a concern;

35
00:02:24,786 --> 00:02:27,357
Coach: they do not establish a personality,

36
00:02:27,357 --> 00:02:31,214
Coach: a hidden motive or a fixed position against demonstrations.

37
00:02:31,564 --> 00:02:34,064
You: You want a short demonstration.

38
00:02:34,414 --> 00:02:39,985
Coach: That summary keeps the proposal, but leaves out its reason and the concern.

39
00:02:39,985 --> 00:02:43,414
Coach: It may be enough for a narrow confirmation;

40
00:02:43,414 --> 00:02:48,128
Coach: it is incomplete if we need to check the whole contribution.

41
00:02:48,478 --> 00:02:53,192
You: You want a brief demonstration so people have time to try,

42
00:02:53,192 --> 00:02:58,764
You: and you are concerned that someone who misses a step might fall behind.

43
00:02:59,114 --> 00:03:03,828
Coach: This version keeps more of the meaning without copying every word.

44
00:03:03,828 --> 00:03:05,971
Coach: It is a possible check,

45
00:03:05,971 --> 00:03:10,257
Coach: not a script you must repeat whenever another person speaks.

46
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:15,321
Coach: Privately choose one detail you would listen for before answering Noah.

47
00:03:15,321 --> 00:03:20,036
Coach: It could be his purpose or the limit of his concern.

48
00:03:20,036 --> 00:03:23,893
Coach: Nothing is recorded, and there is no required wording.

49
00:03:32,243 --> 00:03:34,814
Coach: Useful listening preserves what is there

50
00:03:34,814 --> 00:03:37,814
Coach: and leaves room for what remains unclear.

51
00:03:37,814 --> 00:03:42,100
Coach: Next, we will look more closely at checking your understanding

52
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,243
Coach: without changing the speaker’s point.
